Note: Binary search me 2 index lene parte hai low and high.
      Binary search me 3 hisse hote hai left-half, middle element, right-half.

# Kab kaunsa use kare?  => [mid=(lo+hi)/2;  mid=lo+(hi-lo)/2;]

Situation	                            Approach
1. Small numbers	                    Both work
2. Binary Search	                    Second preferred [mid=lo+(hi-lo)/2]
3. Large integer values	                Second preferred [mid=lo+(hi-lo)/2]
4. Interview / Production code	        Second preferred [mid=lo+(hi-lo)/2]

Reason: Prevents integer overflow that can occur in (lo+hi)/2, provided lo and hi are valid non-negative array indices.
Remember: Jab bhi Binary Search implement karo, default habit rakho:
int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;           =>Isko hi prefer karna hai.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tips: First Occurrence  => go left  :	hi = mid - 1
      Last Occurrence   => go right :   lo = mid + 1

Note: if return 2 array variables then use this
return new int[]{first, last};          =>See in LC.34

----------------------------------------------------
Easy trick to remember:
- Ascending → Small → Big
- Descending → Big → Small

# Quick Revision Notes
1. for swapping:-
Operation	        Condition
1. Ascending	    arr[i] > arr[j] → Swap
2. Descending	    arr[i] < arr[j] → Swap


2. for Binary Search:-
Array order	        Binary Search condition
1. Ascending	    arr[mid] < target → lo = mid + 1
2. Descending	    arr[mid] < target → hi = mid - 1

Note: Descending Binary Search mein direction reverse ho jaati hai.


